# Keep the Docker build context small: the Rust build stage compiles from source,
# so the host's build artifacts and VCS metadata must not be shipped in.
#
# This matters more in a monorepo than it looks. `docker build` uploads the whole
# context to the daemon *before the first instruction runs*, so without this the
# image build spends a minute shipping a multi-gigabyte `target/` it will never
# use — the container compiles from scratch against a different libc anyway.
# `cargo build -p sc-server` then touches only that crate's tree, so the image is
# small because of `sc-server`'s dependencies rather than because of where the
# code lives.
target/
.git/
.smart-coder/
**/*.log

# Read by people, not by the compiler.
docs/
notes/

# The desktop client's assets are the largest non-source tree in the repo, and
# `sc-server` has no relationship to them.
crates/sc-win/assets/
